et` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns a 503.\n\n- **Attempts:** 3 in total by default, set by a new `max_attempts=3` constructor argument.\n- **Backoff:** the wait doubles after each failed attempt. With the default `backoff=0.5`, it waits 0.5s after the first 503 and 1s after the second.\n- **Other errors:** any HTTP error other than 503 is raised straight away with no retry. If all attempts get 503, the last error is raised.\n\nI tested it against a local HTTP server:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503 three times | 503 raised | 3 |\n| 500 | 500 raised | 1 |\n| 200 | data returned | 1 |\n\nOnly HTTP 503 responses are retried. Timeouts and connection failures (`URLError`) are raised on the first attempt; adding them would mean widening the `except` clause.\n\nThere's no test file in the repo, so I didn't add one.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34693, "requests_cache_write": 143539, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7574816, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1640, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 63, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:38:11.375649+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 42.252, "t_checker_s": 2.392, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1652, "tokens_cache_read": 34693, "tokens_cache_write": 14353